erification.json"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+4}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{5}{(x-2)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954117/state.json" "file_sha256" "8258eb37dbbd7a8d4213ea9c431e299ce27b8eba96c31bf2a029f955a927c8db" "basis" 616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954117/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954117/state.json" "file_sha256" "8258eb37dbbd7a8d4213ea9c431e299ce27b8eba96c31bf2a029f955a927c8db" "basis" 616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954117/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-11000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)$ and get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-3x+1=(Ax+B)(x-2)+C({x}^{2}+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)^{2}-3(2)+1 & =(A(2)+B)(2-2)+C({2}^{2}+3) \\\\ 12-6+1 & =7C \\\\ C & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}-3(0)+1 & =(A(0)+B)(0-2)+C({0}^{2}+3) \\\\ 1 & =-2B+3C \\\\ 1 & =-2B+3(1) \\\\ 2B & =2 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}-3(1)+1 & =(A(1)+B)(1-2)+C({1}^{2}+3) \\\\ 1 & =-A-B+4C \\\\ 1 & =-A-1+4(1) \\\\ A & =3-1 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=2,$ $B=1$ and $C=1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-2)}=\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7d4a14efc547d398b8648074ec58aa8ac6cd9ecce42b3262c7a7518819df0b"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{3}{(x-2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{4}{(x-2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+4}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{5}{(x-2)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-11000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-51148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{({x}^{2}+4)x}=\\frac{-x+B}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{1}{x},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-51148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+4)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & =(-x+B)x+({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)+4 & =(-1+B)(1)+({1}^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =-1+B+5 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-51148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7d4a14efc547d398b8648074ec58aa8ac6cd9ecce42b3262c7a7518819df0b"} {"question" "q-51148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-51148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-51148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+3x+4$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)}$ and get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+10x+6=(Ax+B)(x+3)+C({x}^{2}+3x+4).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-3)^{2}+10(-3)+6 & =(A(-3)+B)(-3+3)+C((-3)^{2}+3(-3)+4) \\\\ 36-30+6 & =4C \\\\ 12 & =4C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}+10(0)+6 & =(A(0)+B)(0+3)+C({0}^{2}+3(0)+4) \\\\ 6 & =3B+4C \\\\ 6 & =3B+4(3) \\\\ 3B & =6-12 \\\\ B & =\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}+10(1)+6 & =(A(1)+B)(1+3)+C({1}^{2}+3(1)+4) \\\\ 20 & =4A+4B+8C \\\\ 20 & =4A+4(-2)+8(3) \\\\ 4A & =20+8-24 \\\\ A & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=1,B=-2,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)}=\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7d4a14efc547d398b8648074ec58aa8ac6cd9ecce42b3262c7a7518819df0b"} {"question" "q-102568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2x-1}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}-\\frac{4}{(x+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}-\\frac{2}{(x+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{5}{(x+3)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-29x+34}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}-29x+34}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}-4x+5$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)$ and get\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-29x+34=(Ax+B)(x-3)+C({x}^{2}-4x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(3)^{2}-29(3)+34 & =(A(3)+B)(3-3)+C({3}^{2}-4(3)+5) \\\\ 63-87+34 & =2C \\\\ C & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-29(0)+34 & =(A(0)+B)(0-3)+C({0}^{2}-4(0)+5) \\\\ 34 & =-3B+5C \\\\ 34 & =-3B+5(5) \\\\ 3B & =25-34 \\\\ B & =\\frac{-9}{3} \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1)^{2}-29(1)+34 & =(A(1)+B)(1-3)+C({1}^{2}-4(1)+5) \\\\ 12 & =-2A-2B+2C \\\\ 12 & =-2A-2(-3)+2(5) \\\\ 2A & =-12+6+10 \\\\ A & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=2,B=-3,$ and $C=5.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-29x+34}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)}=\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7d4a14efc547d398b8648074ec58aa8ac6cd9ecce42b3262c7a7518819df0b"} {"question" "q-102574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}-\\frac{3}{(x-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+1}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}-\\frac{4}{(x-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{3}{(x-3)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-102574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-351326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}}$\\,x\\,+$\n{{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $13({x}^{2}+9)$ |  | $13(x-2)$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-351326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{C}{x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+7x+1=(Ax+B)(x-2)+C({x}^{2}+9).\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(2)^{2}+7(2)+1 & =C(4+9) \\\\ 11 & =13C \\\\ C & =\\frac{11}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}+7(0)+1 & =(A(0)+B)(0-2)+\\frac{11}{13}((0)^{2}+9) \\\\ 1 & =-2B+\\frac{99}{13} \\\\ -2B & =-\\frac{86}{13} \\\\ B & =\\frac{43}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(1)^{2}+7(1)+1 & =(A(1)+\\frac{43}{13})(1-2)+\\frac{11}{13}((1)^{2}+9) \\\\ 7 & =-A-\\frac{43}{13}+\\frac{110}{13} \\\\ -A & =\\frac{24}{13} \\\\ A & =-\\frac{24}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{24}{13}x+\\frac{43}{13})}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{(\\frac{11}{13})}{x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24\\,x+43}{13({x}^{2}+9)}+\\frac{11}{13(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-351326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7d4a14efc547d398b8648074ec58aa8ac6cd9ecce42b3262c7a7518819df0b"} {"question" "q-351326" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-351326" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f805617f0867ca353fb8bb29518570184ae88b51eecee217ed8f0baaa410"} {"question" "q-351326" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066924/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab99f8056